      "type": "textEditor",
      "data": {
        "value": "<p><u><strong>SURGICAL PATHOLOGY REPORT</strong></u></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://radiology-flabs.s3.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/1f615af0851f1115f093.png\" alt=\"\"></p>\n<p><br><strong>SPECIMEN :</strong> Skin biopsy for HPE &amp; MT stain.&nbsp;<br><br><strong>CLINICAL&nbsp;</strong><strong>HISTORY :</strong>&nbsp; Collagen vascular disorder.<br><br><strong>GROSS : </strong>Received 1 skin tissue bit measuring 0.4 x 0.3 x 0.2 cm.<br><br><strong>MICROSCOPY : </strong>The histologic sections demonstrate dermal fibrosis with fibroblasts oriented parallel to the surface and vessels oriented perpendicular to the surface epidermis with mild perivascular chronic infiltrate and hyalinized collagen.<br><br><strong>IMPRESSION :</strong> <strong>Skin biopsy for HPE &amp; MT stain: Features are consistent with sclerosing disorder likely hypertrophic scar. </strong></p>\n<p><strong>ADVISED :</strong> Clinical &amp; radiological correlation.</p>\n<p><br><strong>NOTE :</strong> Masson Trichrome stain highlights increased collagen in dermis.</p>",
        "field": "textEditor"
      },
      "_id": "67b86abb7d67ac81b0a0d917"
    }
